# LocalTrace-Nav

## Overview
**LocalTrace-Nav** is an open-source, organic navigation and localization engine designed to replace cold, algorithmic routing systems. Instead of optimizing purely for abstract metrics or commercial throughput, LocalTrace-Nav calculates routes based on **real local purchasing power** and **lived duration**—transforming flat geometric distance into physical, human-scale time-movement.

## Core Philosophy
* **Organic Flow:** Navigation aligned with local realities, supporting small-scale and proximity markets rather than centralized logistics.
* **Duration over Distance:** Distances are measured through the friction of the terrain and the true rhythm of movement.
* **Grounded Mechanics:** Escaping the "headless machine" by tying digital coordinates back to physical agency and local resources.

## Repository Structure
* `README.md`: Project manifest and specifications.
* `engine/`: Core Python calculation scripts for time-movement geometric displacement.
* `matrix/`: Local asset weighting and economic proximity matrices.

## Getting Started
Clone the repository and initialize the Python environment to start mapping local movement vectors:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/sidibemetablok-blip/LocalTrace-Nav.git](https://github.com/sidibemetablok-blip/LocalTrace-Nav.git)
cd LocalTrace-Nav
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
